<div class="keyfind"><b>In three lines</b><ul><li>Start with the problem and who has it.</li><li>Show what you have already tried.</li><li>Be honest about what you do not know.</li></ul><p class="sdgline">SDGs <span class="sdgt sdgc-4" title="SDG 4: Quality Education">4</span><span class="sdgt sdgc-9" title="SDG 9: Industry & Innovation">9</span></p></div>
<p class="note">Sample article: it shows how a Delta publication reads. It contains no survey results or statistics of our own yet.</p>
<h2 id="start-with-the-problem">Start with the problem</h2><p>Reviewers read hundreds of ideas. The strongest ones begin with a clear problem: who has it, where, and what it costs them today. A solution only makes sense once the problem is clear.</p>
<h2 id="show-what-you-have-tried">Show what you have tried</h2><p>Tell us what you have already built, tested or learned, even if it failed. Early evidence, however small, is more convincing than a big promise.</p>
<blockquote>We back people who know what they do not know yet.</blockquote>
<h2 id="be-honest-about-the-gaps">Be honest about the gaps</h2><p>Every idea has unknowns. Naming them shows judgement and helps us match you with the right mentor, lab or partner. Write in Bangla or English, whichever lets you be most precise.</p><p class="tags"><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=idea-portal">#idea-portal</a><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=how-to">#how-to</a></p></article></div></section>
